// The driver's out-of-band machinery, as state: which one auxiliary
// transaction a cycle spends its spare bus time on, what the driver believes
// about torque, and how far a commanded de-torquing has been read back.
//
// A schema for the reason the gate's state is one: every host of these
// decisions keeps them somewhere a cycle boundary can read. The simulated
// driver keeps them in its state slot and the motor driver process keeps the
// same declaration in its own memory, so the two cannot disagree about which
// request is pending, which servos are believed to be holding, or whether a
// sweep has been seen to take.
//
// One module, because one writer owns all of it: the driver's aux machinery
// picks the transaction, records the belief the picked transaction's answer
// changes, and runs the confirmation pass that spends the same slot. Whoever
// only commands the machine reads none of it.
//
// Time is `SyncTime`, never a bare nanosecond count.

#![generate(cpp)]
#![cpp(namespace=brenn_reachy::driver)]

use motion::bus_txn;
use motion::joints;

// The auxiliary slot: one pending host request, the health rotation's place in
// its lap, and the torque belief the slot's answers move.
//
// A slot nothing wrote reads as a driver with no request pending, a rotation at
// row 0 and due, and nothing believed torqued -- which is what a driver that has
// just started is.
schema AuxSlotState
{
    uuid: b0990dbe-7513-4082-b4e5-77617f1aef84;
    fields
    {
        // The pending transaction. Meaningful only when `has_pending`, and
        // copied in rather than referred to: the slot outlives the cycle that
        // offered it, and a re-issue must be the same transaction.
        #0 pending: bus_txn::BusTxn;

        // The correlation number the pending transaction was offered under, and
        // which its outcome echoes. Meaningful only when `has_pending`.
        #1 corr: UInt32;

        // Whether a host request is pending. The queue is one deep because the
        // host that fills it is serial by construction.
        #2 has_pending: Bool;

        // The bus row the health rotation will read next.
        #3 next_row: UInt8;

        // When the last health report was scheduled. Meaningful only when
        // `has_reported`.
        #4 last_report: SyncTime;

        // Whether the rotation has ever been scheduled. Until it has, it is
        // due: a driver that has just started has nothing to say about its
        // servos yet.
        #5 has_reported: Bool;

        // Which servos the driver believes are holding torque. The set the
        // goal masks are drawn from, so a belief names bus rows and nothing
        // else: validating this record refuses a bit no servo answers to,
        // which is the refusal a belief in a tenth servo has to meet
        // somewhere. The set moves only on evidence the driver has itself -- a
        // verified write to a row's torque-enable register, or a confirmed
        // sweep -- because this is what the dead-man is measured against.
        #6 believed_torqued: joints::JointFlags;
    }
}

// A torque-off confirmation pass: how far a commanded de-torquing has been read
// back, and what has been said about it.
//
// A slot nothing wrote reads as a machine that is not running, which asks for
// no read-back and reports nothing until it is begun.
schema TorqueConfirmState
{
    uuid: 51d3c724-2997-4835-90c9-9dc23b2a397d;
    fields
    {
        // Whether a pass is running.
        #0 active: Bool;

        // When the running pass opened, which the budget is measured from.
        // Meaningful only while `active`.
        #1 started: SyncTime;

        // How many rows from row 0 have read back clean in a row. A row found
        // still torqued sends this back to zero, because what is being
        // confirmed is that the machine is off now.
        #2 cursor: UInt8;

        // Whether this pass has already reported that it came clean.
        #3 said_confirmed: Bool;

        // Whether this pass has already reported that its budget ran out. The
        // pass keeps reading afterwards, and still confirms if it comes clean.
        #4 said_unconfirmed: Bool;
    }
}
